   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thanks for understanding about the coffee. On your question: the difference is in who caught it. When the restaurant marks an item unavailable before the order goes out, our system refunds it to your card right away, and that's what happened here. When an item is just left out of the bag, nobody knows until you tell us, so support makes up for it, like we did with the lassi. I'm sorry you weren't told the coffee wasn't coming. I can't see whether a notification was sent, but the refund itself went through.\n\n**Burger Barn (K-6102):** I'm sorry you got a beef burger instead of the veggie burger you ordered. You reported it in time, so I can compensate for the veggie burger ($11.00).\n\nYou chose credit for the lassi, but this one has to go back to your card. Account credit for this item would be $13.20, and with the $17.40 you've already received tonight, that would go over our $25 limit on credit per conversation. In that case our policy is to refund the item to your card.\n\nSo I'll refund **$11.00** to your Visa ending 4242. Is that okay? Once you confirm, I'll process it and we can move on to the Taqueria Luz order."
